# Disney Plus UI - Environment Variables Example
# Copy this file to .env and add your API key

# TMDB API Key (The Movie Database)
# Required for fetching movie and TV show data, images, and trailers
# Get your free API key at: https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
TMDB_API_KEY=your_tmdb_api_key_here

# API Configuration
# The application uses TMDB API to fetch:
# - Movie and TV show metadata (titles, descriptions, ratings)
# - High-quality 4K images (backdrops, posters)
# - Trailer videos from YouTube
# - Genre information
# - Release dates

# API Language
# Currently configured as: en-GB (English - Great Britain)
# Can be changed in scripts/index.js (API_LANGUAGE constant)

# Image Quality Settings
# The application uses the following resolution priority:
# - original: Highest quality, no resolution limit (featured images)
# - w3840: 4K UHD (3840×2160) for thumbnails
# - w1280: HD fallback (1280×720)
# - w780: SD fallback (780×440)

# Usage Instructions:
# 1. Sign up at https://www.themoviedb.org/signup
# 2. Go to Settings > API and generate an API key
# 3. Copy this file to .env
# 4. Replace 'your_tmdb_api_key_here' with your actual API key
# 5. The application will automatically use the API key from .env if available
# 6. If no .env file exists, it will use a hardcoded fallback key
